---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About me"
  description="I'm Nate Barbettini, a founder and technical product builder who distills complex ideas into clear, approachable solutions for developers."
  ogImage="/img/headshot.webp"
  ogImageAlt="Nate Barbettini"
>
  <article class="page-content">
    <img src="/img/headshot.webp" class="headshot" alt="Nate Barbettini" />

    <h4>Hi, I'm Nate.</h4>

    <p> 
      I build products, teams, and systems that turn complicated problems into useful things. 
      My superpower is finding the simple idea hiding inside complexity, then explaining it without making it sound complicated. 
    </p>
    
    <p>
      I like the places where <strong>product, architecture, and technical storytelling overlap</strong>. 
      Over the years, I've been a startup co-founder and CTO, full-stack engineer, developer advocate, open-source contributor, product manager, and Microsoft MVP.
    </p>
    
    <p>
      I'm currently a founder and Member of Technical Staff at <a href="https://arcade.dev">Arcade.dev</a>, where we're building the platform AI agents need to securely take action in the real world.
    </p>

    <h4>Useful things I've built</h4>

    <p>
      I like making things that help developers:
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://mcpdebugger.dev">MCP Debugger</a>, a tool to help Model Context Protocol server devs test their servers as an agent would</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=996OiexHze0">OAuth and OpenID Connect in Plain English</a> (the most-watched OAuth explainer in the world!)</li>
        <li><a href="https://oidcdebugger.com">OIDC Debugger</a>, a tool to easily test OAuth and OpenID Connect flows
        <li><a href="/book/">The Little ASP.NET Core Book</a>, a royalty-free book to help devs learn the ASP.NET Core web framework
      </ul>
    </p>

    <p>
      You can follow me on <a href="https://x.com/nbarbettini">X</a> or <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/nbarbettini">LinkedIn</a> to get notified
      whenever I publish anything new.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
